# The image needs only what `pip install .` builds the wheel from and the Action
# bridge, so everything else stays out of the build context. With no
# .dockerignore, `COPY . /app` put the whole checkout in the image, test
# fixtures included, and Trivy reported the fake mlflow install under
# tests/fixtures/known_vulns as the image's own (#1060).
#
# The wheel reads pyproject.toml, README.md (the long description), LICENSE
# (hatchling's default license files), .gitignore (which hatchling honours when
# it picks the package's files) and agent_audit_kit/. /entrypoint.sh is copied
# by name. tests/test_dockerignore.py pins this list.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!.gitignore
!entrypoint.sh
!agent_audit_kit

# Never package data: bytecode, and the contributor notes the wheel excludes too.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/CLAUDE.md
